  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 121 PM CDT Tue Jun 23 2026\n\nHigh pressure aloft continues to be the dominant weather pattern \nmeaning the dry stretch of weather will continue through the start \nof the upcoming week. These are non-zero chances meaning that an \nisolated, weak shower cannot be ruled out, though it will be not \nwidespread nor a damper to outdoor plans. What will be the main \nthreat will be the Moderate HeatRisk that remains prevalent across \nmost of South Texas as a result of heat index values ranging from \n100-110F. \n\nAside from the heat, this weekend's surface winds become breezier \n(southeast winds at 20-25 mph gusting to 35 mph). This in turn will \nalso result in marine headlines, though these will be decided on \ncloser to the start of the weekend. \n\nMake sure to be ready to apply and reapply the sunscreen/mosquito \nspray/lotions, remain hydrated, and if able, take plenty of breaks \nin the shade/AC.",
